maya: Quick PSA - found a Bun + Deno edge-mode bug with the JS SDK retry path. Auth header disappears on the retry. :confused:

sam: Oof. Minimal repro?

maya: Yup. Using import_map to point to our ESM build in Deno, but Bun sometimes ends up pulling a CJS shim. When a request returns 401 we refresh token and call fetch again, but the second request reaches server with no Authorization.

maya: Repro snippets:````
// import_map.json
{
  "imports": {
    "@redwood/inference": "./node_modules/@redwood/inference/dist/esm/index.js"
  }
}
````

maya: Retry helper is basically:```js
async function retryFetch(url, opts) {
  const res = await fetch(url, opts);
  if (res.status === 401) {
    const token = await refreshToken();
    opts.headers = { ...opts.headers, Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` };
    return fetch(url, opts); // second call loses headers on Bun/Deno
  }
  return res;
}
```

jonah: Which runtimes did you test? Bun stable or edge?

maya: Bun v1.1.x and Deno v1.35 in our edge test harness. Both show Authorization missing in server logs on the retry. Bun's request inspector shows no header on second call. Deno's fetch polyfill we use in tests seems to clone Requests incorrectly.

li: Common pitfall: some fetch implementations consume header bodies or mutate the Headers object. Workaround: always create a fresh Headers or Request before retry. Example:```js
const safeHeaders = new Headers(opts.headers || {});
safeHeaders.set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
return fetch(url, { ...opts, headers: safeHeaders });
```

sam: That aligns with what I've seen. Also our bundler shim for Bun does `globalThis.fetch = (p, o) => nativeFetch(new Request(p, o))` which can consume streams. Changing to `nativeFetch(p, { ...o, headers: new Headers(o?.headers) })` is safer.

jonah: Could this be caused by conditional exports resolving to different helper code between node/edge bundles? If the edge bundle uses a different retry util that relies on Request cloning, we should unify.

maya: Agreed. I hacked a fix: add a tiny internal util cloneImmutableHeaders(headers) used by all retry paths in edge builds. That fixed the repro locally.

devex-bot: Issue opened: RED-DEVEX-472 - "Edge runtimes: preserve Authorization on retry" (assigned to @maya).

infra-bot: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/839 - add header-clone util, update Bun shim, add tests (linux, mac, deno).

sam: Nice. Can we add a small ESM entry export that re-exports cloneImmutableHeaders so conditional-exports don't have to duplicate? Keeps surface minimal.

li: Also add an integration test that runs the exact repro under Bun and Deno and asserts the server sees the header on retry. Mark as optional matrix in CI to avoid flake impact.

maya: I'll add the test, update CHANGELOG under "compatibility fixes", and push a follow-up with notes for the Bun shim. Ping me for review @sam.

jonah: Thanks for the detailed repro, that was fast. Saved me a ton of debugging.

maya: np. I'll update the PR with server logs and a readme for reproducing locally.

sam: Sweet. Once CI green, let's backport the fix to the last minor release branch.
